From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:39:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Don't crash when GLib knows no system config dir on Windows

ardour_config_search_path() builds the "All Users" configuration path
from g_get_system_config_dirs()[0]. GLib returns a NULL-terminated
array that is empty when it cannot resolve the common application data
folder, which happens e.g. when a tool is started from a stripped-down
environment (service, scheduler, `env -i`). Constructing a std::string
from that NULL entry throws std::logic_error, and every Ardour program,
including the headless session utilities, aborts during
ARDOUR::init():

  terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::logic_error'
    what():  basic_string: construction from null is not valid

Skip the All-Users folder when the array has no first entry.
---
 libs/ardour/filesystem_paths.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/ardour/filesystem_paths.cc b/libs/ardour/filesystem_paths.cc
index 0a9e466..384a8db 100644
--- a/libs/ardour/filesystem_paths.cc
+++ b/libs/ardour/filesystem_paths.cc
@@ -250,7 +250,7 @@ ardour_config_search_path ()
 		// Despite its slightly odd name, the above returns a single entry which
 		// corresponds to 'All Users' on Windows (according to the documentation)
 
-		if (all_users_folder) {
+		if (all_users_folder && all_users_folder[0]) {
 			std::string writable_all_users_path = all_users_folder[0];
 			writable_all_users_path += "\\";
 			writable_all_users_path += PROGRAM_NAME;
